  fro-usc:hasChapeauText "The Comptroller of the Currency or the Corporation may reduce the rate of basic pay of a transferred employee—" ;
.
<fro-usc-t12-ch53:r-1-0-4-8-5-5-2>
  rdf:type fro-usc:USC_Chapeau ;
  fro-leg-ref:hasSequenceNumber 2 ;
  fro-usc:hasChapeauText "The funds that, on the day before the transfer date, the Director of the Office of Thrift Supervision (in consultation with the Comptroller of the Currency, the Chairperson of the Corporation, and the Chairman of the Board of Governors) determines are not necessary to dispose of the affairs of the Office of Thrift Supervision under section 5435 of this title and are available to the Office of Thrift Supervision to pay the expenses of the Office of Thrift Supervision—" ;
  fro-usc:hasReferenceText "/us/usc/t12/s5435" ;
  fro-usc:refers_toLevel fro-usc-t12-ch53:id83a40226-1df7-11e6-87ee-8e4a3ab90f2a ;
.
<fro-usc-t12-ch53:r-1-0-4-8-5-6-2-2>
  rdf:type fro-usc:USC_Chapeau ;
  fro-leg-ref:hasSequenceNumber 2 ;
  fro-usc:hasChapeauText "During the 90-day period beginning on the transfer date, the Director of the Office of Thrift Supervision—" ;
.
<fro-usc-t12-ch53:r-1-0-4-8-5-6-2-3-1>
  rdf:type fro-usc:USC_Chapeau ;
  fro-leg-ref:hasSequenceNumber 1 ;
  fro-leg-ref:refers_toNote fro-usc-t12-ch53:fn002488 ;
  fro-usc:hasChapeauText "shall, solely for the purpose of winding up the affairs of the Office of Thrift Supervision relating to any function transferred to the Office of the Comptroller of the Currency, the Corporation, or the Board of Governors under this title—  1" ;
.
<fro-usc-t12-ch53:r-1-0-4-8-5-6-3-2-2>
  rdf:type fro-usc:USC_Chapeau ;
  fro-leg-ref:hasSequenceNumber 2 ;
  fro-usc:hasChapeauText "Notwithstanding the transfer of functions under this part, during the 90-day period beginning on the transfer date, the Director of the Office of Thrift Supervision shall retain and may exercise any authority vested in the Director of the Office of Thrift Supervision on the day before the transfer date, only to the extent necessary—" ;
.
<fro-usc-t12-ch53:r-1-0-4-8-5-6-3-3-2>
  rdf:type fro-usc:USC_Chapeau ;
  fro-leg-ref:hasSequenceNumber 2 ;
  fro-usc:hasChapeauText "For purposes of paragraph (1), the Director of the Office of Thrift Supervision shall, during the 90-day period beginning on the transfer date, continue to be—" ;
.
<fro-usc-t12-ch53:r-1-0-4-8-5-7-2>
  rdf:type fro-usc:USC_Chapeau ;
  fro-leg-ref:hasSequenceNumber 2 ;
  fro-leg-ref:refers_toNote fro-usc-t12-ch53:fn002489 ;
  fro-usc:hasChapeauText "Any agency, department, or other instrumentality of the United States, and any successor to any such agency, department, or instrumentality, that was, before the transfer date, providing support services to the Office of Thrift Supervision in connection with functions transferred to the Office of the Comptroller of the Currency, the Corporation or the Board of Governors under this title, 1 shall—" ;
.
<fro-usc-t12-ch53:r-1-0-4-8-5-8-3-2>
  rdf:type fro-usc:USC_Chapeau ;
  fro-leg-ref:hasSequenceNumber 2 ;
  fro-usc:hasChapeauText "Within 60 days of receiving the plan required under subsection (a), the Inspectors General of the Department of the Treasury, the Corporation, and the Board of Governors shall jointly provide a written report to the Board of Governors, the Corporation, the Office of the Comptroller of the Currency, and the Office of Thrift Supervision and shall submit a copy to the Committee on Banking, Housing, and Urban Affairs of the Senate and the Committee on Financial Services of the House of Representatives detailing whether the plan conforms with the provisions of sections 301 through 326, and the provisions of the amendments made by such sections, including—" ;
.
<fro-usc-t12-ch53:r-1-0-4-8-6-2-2>
  rdf:type fro-usc:USC_Chapeau ;
  fro-leg-ref:hasSequenceNumber 2 ;
  fro-usc:hasChapeauText "Notwithstanding the Federal Deposit Insurance Act ( 12 U.S.C. 1811 et seq.), the Bank Holding Company Act of 1956 ( 12 U.S.C. 1841 et seq.), or any other provision of Federal or State law, a savings association that becomes a bank may—" ;
  fro-usc:hasReferenceText "/us/usc/t12/s1811" ;
  fro-usc:hasReferenceText "/us/usc/t12/s1841" ;
.
<fro-usc-t12-ch53:r-1-0-4-8-6-3-3-3-2>
  rdf:type fro-usc:USC_Chapeau ;
  fro-leg-ref:hasSequenceNumber 2 ;
  fro-usc:hasChapeauText "Each Director shall develop standards for—" ;
.
<fro-usc-t12-ch53:r-1-0-4-8-6-3-4-4-3-3-2>
  rdf:type fro-usc:USC_Chapeau ;
  fro-leg-ref:hasSequenceNumber 2 ;
  fro-usc:hasChapeauText "Upon receipt of a recommendation under clause (i), the agency administrator may—" ;
.
<fro-usc-t12-ch53:r-1-0-4-8-6-3-6-2>
  rdf:type fro-usc:USC_Chapeau ;
  fro-leg-ref:hasSequenceNumber 2 ;
  fro-usc:hasChapeauText "Each Office shall submit to Congress an annual report regarding the actions taken by the agency and the Office pursuant to this section, which shall include—" ;
.
<fro-usc-t12-ch53:r-1-0-4-8-6-3-7-2>
  rdf:type fro-usc:USC_Chapeau ;
  fro-leg-ref:hasSequenceNumber 2 ;
  fro-usc:hasChapeauText "Each agency shall take affirmative steps to seek diversity in the workforce of the agency at all levels of the agency in a manner consistent with applicable law. Such steps shall include—" ;
.
<fro-usc-t12-ch53:r-1-0-4-8-6-3-8-2>
  rdf:type fro-usc:USC_Chapeau ;
  fro-leg-ref:hasSequenceNumber 2 ;
  fro-usc:hasChapeauText "For purposes of this section, the following definitions shall apply:" ;
.
<fro-usc-t12-ch53:r-1-0-4-8-6-3-8-3-2>
  rdf:type fro-usc:USC_Chapeau ;
  fro-leg-ref:hasSequenceNumber 2 ;
  fro-usc:hasChapeauText "The term “agency” means—" ;
.
<fro-usc-t12-ch53:r-1-0-4-9-12-2-2>
  rdf:type fro-usc:USC_Chapeau ;
  fro-leg-ref:hasSequenceNumber 2 ;
  fro-usc:hasChapeauText "The Commodity Futures Trading Commission shall consult with the Board of Governors—" ;
.
<fro-usc-t12-ch53:r-1-0-4-9-12-3-2>
  rdf:type fro-usc:USC_Chapeau ;
  fro-leg-ref:hasSequenceNumber 2 ;
  fro-usc:hasChapeauText "The Commission shall consult with the Board of Governors—" ;
.
<fro-usc-t12-ch53:r-1-0-4-9-13-2>
  rdf:type fro-usc:USC_Chapeau ;
  fro-leg-ref:hasDate "2010-07-21"^^xsd:date ;
  fro-leg-ref:hasSequenceNumber 2 ;
  fro-leg-ref:refers_toNote fro-usc-t12-ch53:fn002500 ;
  fro-usc:hasChapeauText "The Commodity Futures Trading Commission and the Commission shall coordinate with the Board of Governors to jointly develop risk management supervision programs for designated clearing entities. Not later than 1 year after July 21, 2010 , the Commodity Futures Trading Commission, the Commission, and the Board of Governors shall submit a joint report to the Committee on Banking, Housing, and Urban Affairs and the Committee on Agriculture, Nutrition, and Forestry of the Senate, and the Committee on Financial Services and the Committee on Agriculture of the House of Representatives recommendations  1 for—" ;
.
<fro-usc-t12-ch53:r-1-0-4-9-2-2-2>
  rdf:type fro-usc:USC_Chapeau ;
  fro-leg-ref:hasSequenceNumber 2 ;
  fro-usc:hasChapeauText "Congress finds the following:" ;
.
<fro-usc-t12-ch53:r-1-0-4-9-2-2-6-1>
  rdf:type fro-usc:USC_Chapeau ;
  fro-leg-ref:hasSequenceNumber 1 ;
  fro-usc:hasChapeauText "Enhancements to the regulation and supervision of systemically important financial market utilities and the conduct of systemically important payment, clearing, and settlement activities by financial institutions are necessary—" ;
.
<fro-usc-t12-ch53:r-1-0-4-9-2-3-2>
  rdf:type fro-usc:USC_Chapeau ;
  fro-leg-ref:hasSequenceNumber 2 ;
  fro-usc:hasChapeauText "The purpose of this subchapter is to mitigate systemic risk in the financial system and promote financial stability by—" ;
.
<fro-usc-t12-ch53:r-1-0-4-9-2-3-3-1>
  rdf:type fro-usc:USC_Chapeau ;
  fro-leg-ref:hasSequenceNumber 1 ;
  fro-usc:hasChapeauText "authorizing the Board of Governors to promote uniform standards for the—" ;
.
<fro-usc-t12-ch53:r-1-0-4-9-2-5-0-1-6>
  rdf:type fro-usc:USC_QuotedContent ;
  fro-usc:hasQuotedContentText "“This title [enacting this subchapter] is effective as of the date of enactment of this Act [ July 21, 2010 ].”" ;
  fro-usc:hasReferenceText "/us/pl/111/203/tVIII" ;
.
<fro-usc-t12-ch53:r-1-0-4-9-3-10-2-2>
  rdf:type fro-usc:USC_Chapeau ;
  fro-leg-ref:hasSequenceNumber 2 ;
  fro-usc:hasChapeauText "The term “Supervisory Agency” means the Federal agency that has primary jurisdiction over a designated financial market utility under Federal banking, securities, or commodity futures laws, as follows:" ;
.
<fro-usc-t12-ch53:r-1-0-4-9-3-2>
  rdf:type fro-usc:USC_Chapeau ;
  fro-leg-ref:hasSequenceNumber 2 ;
  fro-usc:hasChapeauText "In this subchapter, the following definitions shall apply:" ;
.
<fro-usc-t12-ch53:r-1-0-4-9-3-3-2>
  rdf:type fro-usc:USC_Chapeau ;
  fro-leg-ref:hasSequenceNumber 2 ;
  fro-usc:hasChapeauText "The term “appropriate financial regulator” means—" ;
.
<fro-usc-t12-ch53:r-1-0-4-9-3-7-2-2>
  rdf:type fro-usc:USC_Chapeau ;
  fro-leg-ref:hasSequenceNumber 2 ;
  fro-usc:hasChapeauText "The term “financial institution” means—" ;
.
<fro-usc-t12-ch53:r-1-0-4-9-3-8-3-2>
  rdf:type fro-usc:USC_Chapeau ;
  fro-leg-ref:hasSequenceNumber 2 ;
  fro-usc:hasChapeauText "The term “financial market utility” does not include—" ;
.
<fro-usc-t12-ch53:r-1-0-4-9-3-9-3-2>
  rdf:type fro-usc:USC_Chapeau ;
  fro-leg-ref:hasSequenceNumber 2 ;
  fro-usc:hasChapeauText "For the purposes of subparagraph (A), the term “financial transaction” includes—" ;
.
<fro-usc-t12-ch53:r-1-0-4-9-3-9-4-2>
  rdf:type fro-usc:USC_Chapeau ;
  fro-leg-ref:hasSequenceNumber 2 ;
  fro-usc:hasChapeauText "When conducted with respect to a financial transaction, payment, clearing, and settlement activities may include—" ;
.
<fro-usc-t12-ch53:r-1-0-4-9-4-2-3-2>
  rdf:type fro-usc:USC_Chapeau ;
  fro-leg-ref:hasSequenceNumber 2 ;
  fro-usc:hasChapeauText "In determining whether a financial market utility or payment, clearing, or settlement activity is, or is likely to become, systemically important, the Council shall take into consideration the following:" ;
.
<fro-usc-t12-ch53:r-1-0-4-9-5-2-2-2>
  rdf:type fro-usc:USC_Chapeau ;
  fro-leg-ref:hasSequenceNumber 2 ;
  fro-usc:hasChapeauText "Except as provided in paragraph (2), the Board of Governors, by rule or order, and in consultation with the Council and the Supervisory Agencies, shall prescribe risk management standards, taking into consideration relevant international standards and existing prudential requirements, governing—" ;
.
<fro-usc-t12-ch53:r-1-0-4-9-5-2-3-2-2>
  rdf:type fro-usc:USC_Chapeau ;
  fro-leg-ref:hasSequenceNumber 2 ;
  fro-usc:hasChapeauText "The Commodity Futures Trading Commission and the Commission may each prescribe regulations, in consultation with the Council and the Board of Governors, containing risk management standards, taking into consideration relevant international standards and existing prudential requirements, for those designated clearing entities and financial institutions engaged in designated activities for which each is the Supervisory Agency or the appropriate financial regulator, governing—" ;
.
<fro-usc-t12-ch53:r-1-0-4-9-5-3-2>
  rdf:type fro-usc:USC_Chapeau ;
  fro-leg-ref:hasSequenceNumber 2 ;
  fro-usc:hasChapeauText "The objectives and principles for the risk management standards prescribed under subsection (a) shall be to—" ;
.
<fro-usc-t12-ch53:r-1-0-4-9-5-4-2>
  rdf:type fro-usc:USC_Chapeau ;
  fro-leg-ref:hasSequenceNumber 2 ;
  fro-usc:hasChapeauText "The standards prescribed under subsection (a) may address areas such as—" ;
.
<fro-usc-t12-ch53:r-1-0-4-9-5-5-2>
  rdf:type fro-usc:USC_Chapeau ;
  fro-leg-ref:hasSequenceNumber 2 ;
  fro-usc:hasChapeauText "Except as provided in subsections (e) and (f) of section 5466 of this title , nothing in this subchapter shall be construed to permit the Council or the Board of Governors to take any action or exercise any authority granted to the Commodity Futures Trading Commission under section 2(h) of title 7 or the Securities and Exchange Commission under section 78c–3(a) of title 15 , including—" ;
  fro-usc:hasReferenceText "/us/usc/t12/s5466" ;
  fro-usc:hasReferenceText "/us/usc/t15/s78c–3/a" ;
  fro-usc:hasReferenceText "/us/usc/t7/s2/h" ;
.
<fro-usc-t12-ch53:r-1-0-4-9-6-6-2-4-2>
  rdf:type fro-usc:USC_Chapeau ;
  fro-leg-ref:hasSequenceNumber 2 ;
  fro-usc:hasChapeauText "The notice of a proposed change shall describe—" ;
.
<fro-usc-t12-ch53:r-1-0-4-9-6-6-2-6-2>
  rdf:type fro-usc:USC_Chapeau ;
  fro-leg-ref:hasSequenceNumber 2 ;
  fro-usc:hasChapeauText "The Supervisory Agency shall notify the designated financial market utility of any objection regarding the proposed change within 60 days from the later of—" ;
.
<fro-usc-t12-ch53:r-1-0-4-9-6-6-2-8-2>
  rdf:type fro-usc:USC_Chapeau ;
  fro-leg-ref:hasSequenceNumber 2 ;
  fro-usc:hasChapeauText "A designated financial market utility may implement a change if it has not received an objection to the proposed change within 60 days of the later of—" ;
.
<fro-usc-t12-ch53:r-1-0-4-9-6-6-3-2-2>
  rdf:type fro-usc:USC_Chapeau ;
  fro-leg-ref:hasSequenceNumber 2 ;
  fro-usc:hasChapeauText "A designated financial market utility may implement a change that would otherwise require advance notice under this subsection if it determines that—" ;
.
<fro-usc-t12-ch53:r-1-0-4-9-6-6-3-4-2>
  rdf:type fro-usc:USC_Chapeau ;
  fro-leg-ref:hasSequenceNumber 2 ;
  fro-usc:hasChapeauText "In addition to the information required for changes requiring advance notice, the notice of an emergency change shall describe—" ;
.
<fro-usc-t12-ch53:r-1-0-4-9-7-2-2>
  rdf:type fro-usc:USC_Chapeau ;
  fro-leg-ref:hasSequenceNumber 2 ;
  fro-usc:hasChapeauText "Notwithstanding any other provision of law and subject to subsection (d), the Supervisory Agency shall conduct examinations of a designated financial market utility at least once annually in order to determine the following:" ;
.
<fro-usc-t12-ch53:r-1-0-4-9-7-2-7-1>
  rdf:type fro-usc:USC_Chapeau ;
  fro-leg-ref:hasSequenceNumber 1 ;
  fro-usc:hasChapeauText "The designated financial market utility’s compliance with—" ;
.
<fro-usc-t12-ch53:r-1-0-4-9-7-6-5-2>
  rdf:type fro-usc:USC_Chapeau ;
  fro-leg-ref:hasSequenceNumber 2 ;
  fro-usc:hasChapeauText "Upon an affirmative vote by a majority of the Council in favor of the Board of Governors’ recommendation under paragraph (3), the Council may require the Supervisory Agency to—" ;
.
<fro-usc-t12-ch53:r-1-0-4-9-7-7-2-2>
  rdf:type fro-usc:USC_Chapeau ;
  fro-leg-ref:hasSequenceNumber 2 ;
  fro-usc:hasChapeauText "The Board of Governors may, after consulting with the Supervisory Agency and upon an affirmative vote by a majority the Council, take enforcement action against a designated financial market utility if the Board of Governors has reasonable cause to conclude that—" ;
.
<fro-usc-t12-ch53:r-1-0-4-9-7-7-2-3-1>
  rdf:type fro-usc:USC_Chapeau ;
  fro-leg-ref:hasSequenceNumber 1 ;
  fro-usc:hasChapeauText "either—" ;
.
<fro-usc-t12-ch53:r-1-0-4-9-8-2-2>
  rdf:type fro-usc:USC_Chapeau ;
  fro-leg-ref:hasSequenceNumber 2 ;
  fro-usc:hasChapeauText "The appropriate financial regulator is authorized to examine a financial institution subject to the standards prescribed under section 5464(a) of this title for a designated activity in order to determine the following:" ;
  fro-usc:hasReferenceText "/us/usc/t12/s5464/a" ;
.
<fro-usc-t12-ch53:r-1-0-4-9-8-5-2-2-2>
  rdf:type fro-usc:USC_Chapeau ;
  fro-leg-ref:hasSequenceNumber 2 ;
  fro-usc:hasChapeauText "The appropriate financial regulator may request the Board of Governors to conduct or participate in an examination of a financial institution subject to the standards prescribed under section 5464(a) of this title for a designated activity in order to assess the compliance of such financial institution with—" ;
  fro-usc:hasReferenceText "/us/usc/t12/s5464/a" ;
.
<fro-usc-t12-ch53:r-1-0-4-9-8-6-2-2>
  rdf:type fro-usc:USC_Chapeau ;
  fro-leg-ref:hasSequenceNumber 2 ;
  fro-usc:hasChapeauText "Notwithstanding any other provision of law, the Board of Governors may—" ;
.
<fro-usc-t12-ch53:r-1-0-4-9-8-6-3-2-2>
  rdf:type fro-usc:USC_Chapeau ;
  fro-leg-ref:hasSequenceNumber 2 ;
  fro-usc:hasChapeauText "The Board of Governors may exercise the authority described in paragraph (1)(A) only if the Board of Governors has—" ;
.
<fro-usc-t12-ch53:r-1-0-4-9-8-6-3-2-6-1>
  rdf:type fro-usc:USC_Chapeau ;
  fro-leg-ref:hasSequenceNumber 1 ;
  fro-usc:hasChapeauText "either—" ;
.
<fro-usc-t12-ch53:r-1-0-4-9-8-6-3-3-2>
  rdf:type fro-usc:USC_Chapeau ;
  fro-leg-ref:hasSequenceNumber 2 ;
  fro-usc:hasChapeauText "The Board of Governors may exercise the authority described in paragraph (1)(B) only if the Board of Governors has—" ;
.
<fro-usc-t12-ch53:r-1-0-4-9-8-6-3-3-5-1>
  rdf:type fro-usc:USC_Chapeau ;
  fro-leg-ref:hasSequenceNumber 1 ;
  fro-usc:hasChapeauText "either—" ;
.
<fro-usc-t12-ch53:r-1-0-4-9-9-3-3-2>
  rdf:type fro-usc:USC_Chapeau ;
  fro-leg-ref:hasSequenceNumber 2 ;
  fro-usc:hasChapeauText "The Board of Governors and the Council may each require 1 or more financial institutions subject to the standards prescribed under section 5464(a) of this title for a designated activity to submit, in such frequency and form as deemed necessary by the Board of Governors or the Council, reports and data to the Board of Governors and the Council solely with respect to the conduct of the designated activity and solely to assess whether—" ;
  fro-usc:hasReferenceText "/us/usc/t12/s5464/a" ;
.
<fro-usc-t12-ch53:r-1-0-4-9-9-6-2-2>
  rdf:type fro-usc:USC_Chapeau ;
  fro-leg-ref:hasSequenceNumber 2 ;
  fro-usc:hasChapeauText "Notwithstanding any other provision of law, the Board of Governors, the Council, the appropriate financial regulator, and any Supervisory Agency are authorized to—" ;
.
